# WESTINGEN Project Rules

## Purpose

This project exists solely to support a job application. It demonstrates backend development skills with Python and Flask in a production-like but minimal context.

## Non-Goals

The following are explicitly NOT included:
- Authentication and authorization
- Production security hardening
- Microservices architecture
- React, Next.js, or any SPA framework
- Docker containerization
- Unit tests or test coverage
- CI/CD pipelines
- Advanced monitoring or logging

## Architecture Rules

- One Flask application
- One PostgreSQL database
- Server-rendered UI (Jinja templates) or static HTML only
- Maximum 10 API endpoints
- Maximum 20 dependencies

## Coding Rules

- Explicit code over abstractions
- No premature optimization
- Simple naming over clever naming
- If unsure, choose the simpler solution
- No over-engineering

## Demo Rules

- Must run locally in under 5 minutes
- README-first mindset (recruiter-friendly, not developer-ego-driven)
- Everything must be runnable with minimal setup
- Focus on credibility and understandability over technical impressiveness
